anchor.description:
Decoded anchor entity (by display name) the question is about;
retrieval co-binds its bounded neighborhood (`graph_anchor`, boost
mode). `None` when the question anchors on nothing retrievable.

relation.description:
Decoded (or signature-forced) relation the question pivots on;
retrieval constrains assertion scoring to it. `None` when the question
names no relation.

runner.description:
The app whose answers the run checked (`POST /v1/evals/run/answers`);
absent for a run of the server's own Ask. Each app's runs are a
series of their own.

trained_at_commit_seq.description:
The snapshot the run was derived from. Trainers MUST train on data
≤ this commit and evaluate on > it (the temporal-split obligation);
recording it here is what lets audits verify the split.

oneOf.description:
The batch decision that accepted or dismissed it
(`POST /v1/ontology/suggestions/accept-batch` or `/dismiss-batch`);
absent for a decision on the suggestion alone.

asserted.description:
Omitted on ordinary patches preserves the selected support's state;
new support defaults true. Complete scope replacement requires this
explicitly alongside the full tuple, even for an existing claim.

ReviewQuestion.description:
What an item asks, by kind:
- `value`: `property`, the proposed `value`, its `unit` and `confidence`;
- `choice`: `options`, and the `proposed` option with its `confidence`;
- `grade`: the `output` to grade, `options` (the grades) and `proposed`;
- `answer`: the `prompt`.

fields.description:
Entity attributes to project onto each entity hit from the same graph
snapshot used for ranking. Omitted or empty keeps the lean response;
`"*"` or `"all"` returns every attribute.

active_revision.description:
The settings revision the workflow runs on (`wrev_…`;
`GET /v1/workflows/named/revisions` lists its history). Absent for
`search.embed` and `ontology.fit`, which keep no revisions.

counters.description:
The turn result's `counters` (whole numbers by name, at most 32);
for a step of the Rust path what it added to the workflow's
counters.
